Z||000002||frontal lobe||03-01-2001||06:57 PM||||Personal taste-I find the Celica line to consistently be one of the wierdest-styled cars of all time.  But they have that typical Toyota quality and are pretty peppy.  No idea if the tranny could be put in a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||03-01-2001||07:14 PM||||The transmission would be hard to put into a Fiero. Might as well do the whole drivetrain.  I'd like to graft a Celica drivetrain into a first or third gen MR2. That would make a slick ride.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||03-01-2001||08:42 PM||||memories.... my very 1st car was a '77 celica!  (showing age here)back in '83.  usually one would thing that getting a 6 year old car as a new ride, as being a deal... not  this puppy, it look more like a 20 yo car.  what a POS.<P>as for the new celicas, they are very nice.  i haven't driven one yet, but have considered it as a replacement for my cherokee, when the lease is up. (that is if i don't get a '65 tbird convertible)<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||03-01-2001||10:25 PM||||The new Celica's are a big improvement over the previous generation Celica.  My personal opinion is that they are the best sports coupe on the market.  I like the styling better than either the Eclipse or Cougar.  Reliability should be bettere than those two and its probably the best handling and most fun to drive (although I have not driven it yet).  My friends father owned an old 280Z for years, but decided to sell it when he bought a '00 Celica GTS.  Despite the lack of low end Torque, he is very satisfied with its power!  ||||reg||1
